# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BAZAAR - build context exclusions
#
# The image is built from the repository root (see apps/api/Dockerfile), so
# without this the context is the whole workspace including every node_modules
# and .next directory - hundreds of megabytes uploaded to the daemon before the
# first instruction runs.
#
# Excluding node_modules is not only about size: the host's tree is resolved for
# Windows and would overwrite the Linux one installed inside the image.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets. `.env.example` is the one that ships; a real .env baked into a layer
# is readable by anyone who can pull the image, and deleting it in a later
# instruction does not remove it from the earlier one.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.github
.vscode
.idea

# Documentation and audit output - none of it is needed to build or run.
*.md
!apps/api/README.md
.lighthouseci
docker-compose.yml
